Homepage: https://bnk989.github.io/AutoLang/
Description: fixes text typed in the wrong keyboard layout
 AutoLang is an IBus input method for people who type in two alphabets, such
 as English and Hebrew. It types in all of your layouts itself: a word typed
 in the wrong one ("akuo") is replaced by what you meant ("שלום") when you
 finish it, and typing carries on in that language. Double-tap Shift to undo
 a correction or convert what you just typed.
 .
 Everything runs locally: no network, no account, no telemetry. Typed text is
 never stored or logged.
